  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Given that $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{4}{3}$ and $\\theta$ is in Quadrant III, find each of the following:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{24}{25}$",
          "worked": "In Quadrant III, both sine and cosine are negative. A reference triangle has legs 4 and 3 and hypotenuse $\\sqrt{4^2+3^2}=5$, so $\\sin\\theta=-\\frac45$ and $\\cos\\theta=-\\frac35$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin 2\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=2\\left(-\\frac45\\right)\\left(-\\frac35\\right)\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=\\frac{24}{25}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{7}{25}$",
          "worked": "The reference triangle has hypotenuse 5. Since $\\theta$ is in Quadrant III, $\\sin\\theta=-\\frac45$ and $\\cos\\theta=-\\frac35$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos 2\\theta&=\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=\\left(-\\frac35\\right)^2-\\left(-\\frac45\\right)^2\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=\\frac9{25}-\\frac{16}{25}\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=-\\frac7{25}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{24}{7}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{2\\left(\\frac43\\right)}{1-\\left(\\frac43\\right)^2}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{\\frac83}{-\\frac79}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=-\\frac{24}{7}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
  },
